    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0201" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/471: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-26T16:00:00+01:00">August 26, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 26—1:50 a.m]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>402. Foreign Office has just telephoned that negative Japanese note on British
                    memorandum has been delivered and a copy will be forwarded me this
                        evening.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d104-f1"/> In the meantime they ask urgently
                    whether a copy of my memorandum to them based on your 211, August 14, 7 p.m.,
                    may be made available to the Japanese and French, and the press informed [of]
                    its existence. In the latter case kindly indicate <pb facs="0202" n="100"
                        xml:id="pg100"/> whether, and if so, how much of its contents may be made
                    public. The British hope for an answer that will enable them to make the press
                    announcement tomorrow morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
